:answer/id #uuid "f75aa233-1836-53e9-b702-26aa5f586d93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/65/65dfb1343beb471ab76556f9e5a5614b3c34d731ac8a4f0b784e2aa36e6e99d0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395186} {:answer/id #uuid "5d6f227a-b324-5ed1-bbcb-aa7d362498bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0b/0bdd1639343c7ad57ca69190e4e035b9c7a52f5820c99d81461146427bc1e123.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c273ef8b-de15-57c8-95a2-e369aea97f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/49911d2a6e8e7f8bb13524a604507db0b797b06d237665081b8823aeb596e2da.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395185} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3448bae-8bc3-5354-a5fa-3b084382276a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6760ce21-745a-540e-98c2-9541661dd438" :question/math-academy-id "q-96721" :question/problem "![](images/a7/a7c0dbc5a27bdb0da8b5e319c52a38af85c09a75e90c957e9f7be3822cdb6d90.png)\n\nWhich of the following diagrams depicts the lines representing the principal axes of the quadratic curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The principal axes of a curve define a coordinate system in which the curve can be represented by its (simplest) canonical equation. \n\nOur curve is a hyperbola. This curve will have the canonical equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nif one axis passes through the vertices of the hyperbola and the other axis is the perpendicular bisector of the segment connecting the two vertices.\n\n![](images/49/49911d2a6e8e7f8bb13524a604507db0b797b06d237665081b8823aeb596e2da.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 1759218636